From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Subject: [PATCH] leds: lgm-sso: align driver with leds-lgm.yaml binding

The leds-lgm.yaml binding documents the per-LED subnode container as
"led-controller" and the per-LED GPIO property as "led-gpios"
(updated by Rob Herring in 121164481b79). The driver, however, looks
for a child node named "ssoled" and resolves the GPIO via con_id NULL,
which translates to property names "gpios" / "gpio". As a result, any
DT that follows the documented binding gets no LEDs registered.

Look up the documented "led-controller" subnode first, falling back
to "ssoled"; resolve each LED's GPIO with con_id "led" first, falling
back to NULL. Both fallbacks preserve compatibility with existing
devicetrees (DT is ABI).

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
--- a/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
@@ -637,8 +637,12 @@ __sso_led_dt_parse(struct sso_led_priv *
 		led->priv = priv;
 		desc = &led->desc;
 
-		led->gpiod = devm_fwnode_gpiod_get(dev, fwnode_child, NULL,
+		led->gpiod = devm_fwnode_gpiod_get(dev, fwnode_child, "led",
 						   GPIOD_ASIS, NULL);
+		if (PTR_ERR(led->gpiod) == -ENOENT)
+			led->gpiod = devm_fwnode_gpiod_get(dev, fwnode_child,
+							   NULL, GPIOD_ASIS,
+							   NULL);
 		if (IS_ERR(led->gpiod)) {
 			ret = dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(led->gpiod), "led: get gpio fail!\n");
 			goto __dt_err;
@@ -728,7 +732,9 @@ static int sso_led_dt_parse(struct sso_l
 	if (!count)
 		return 0;
 
-	fw_ssoled = fwnode_get_named_child_node(fwnode, "ssoled");
+	fw_ssoled = fwnode_get_named_child_node(fwnode, "led-controller");
+	if (!fw_ssoled)
+		fw_ssoled = fwnode_get_named_child_node(fwnode, "ssoled");
 	if (fw_ssoled) {
 		ret = __sso_led_dt_parse(priv, fw_ssoled);
 		fwnode_handle_put(fw_ssoled);
